notes: >
  This is Google's own official PyTorch port of the legacy TimesFM-1.0
  architecture (decoder-only, causal, input patch length 32, output patch
  length 128, per-patch instance normalization via _forward_transform /
  _reverse_transform, residual input/output blocks, RMSNorm transformer
  layers, quantile + point output heads). It is not used with Google's
  released 1.0 checkpoint weights; this project builds reduced (~17M and
  ~70M parameter) configs of PatchedTimeSeriesDecoder / TimesFMConfig and
  trains them from a random initialization on GiftEvalPretrain, per the
  "reduced configuration" instruction in
  notes/05-timesfm-pretraining-loss-space-plan.md. timesfm_model.py wraps
  this class rather than reimplementing the architecture, so the parity test
  (tests/test_timesfm_model.py) is a determinism/shape/causality/
  instance-norm-invertibility check on that wrapper, not a bit-exact
  comparison against Google's released checkpoint.
